      "id": "t134",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1387.4,
      "y": 1450.0,
      "width": 445.2,
      "height": 525.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "text": "docs/findings.md — results so far\n\n⚠  F1–F3d ARE PROVISIONAL AND MUST BE RE-RUN.\nEvery number below came from --experts surrogate:\nMLPs on three hand-built views that were DESIGNED to\ndegrade under different acquisition defects. Routing\nwas therefore tested on a bench where the premise it\ndepends on was authored rather than observed.\n\nTHE CLAIM (falsifiable):\nB6 beats B4 on AURC in the low-quality cohort, with a\npaired-bootstrap CI excluding zero. If the CI crosses\nzero, routing did not help — and that is the result\nwe report.\n\nOBSERVED (surrogates · phantoms · single seed):\n· routing came out WORSE under shift\n  (AURC +0.05 … +0.06)\n· cause 1 — the router never saw the target domain\n  → --calib-target-fraction 0.15\n  gate coverage 56% → 89%   (FIXED)\n· cause 2 — the router is overparameterised:\n  120 params on ~40 calibration cases\n  → --router-shared cuts it to 24   (OPEN)\n\nReal ResNet/ViT backbones have genuinely different\ninductive biases and give the premise its first fair\ntest:\n  cgate --experts torch --arch resnet50\n        --pretrained --n-cases 400",
      "originalText": "docs/findings.md — results so far\n\n⚠  F1–F3d ARE PROVISIONAL AND MUST BE RE-RUN.\nEvery number below came from --experts surrogate:\nMLPs on three hand-built views that were DESIGNED to\ndegrade under different acquisition defects. Routing\nwas therefore tested on a bench where the premise it\ndepends on was authored rather than observed.\n\nTHE CLAIM (falsifiable):\nB6 beats B4 on AURC in the low-quality cohort, with a\npaired-bootstrap CI excluding zero. If the CI crosses\nzero, routing did not help — and that is the result\nwe report.\n\nOBSERVED (surrogates · phantoms · single seed):\n· routing came out WORSE under shift\n  (AURC +0.05 … +0.06)\n· cause 1 — the router never saw the target domain\n  → --calib-target-fraction 0.15\n  gate coverage 56% → 89%   (FIXED)\n· cause 2 — the router is overparameterised:\n  120 params on ~40 calibration cases\n  → --router-shared cuts it to 24   (OPEN)\n\nReal ResNet/ViT backbones have genuinely different\ninductive biases and give the premise its first fair\ntest:\n  cgate --experts torch --arch resnet50\n        --pretrained --n-cases 400",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
